---
title: Newsletter
layout: home
description: The archive of a letter — what it is, a form to join it, and every issue that has gone out, numbered. A newsletter's back catalogue is the best argument for subscribing to it.
eyebrow: Collections · Newsletter
source: src/components/collection.css · field.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Newsletter · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-wrap-wide im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
	<header class="im-letterhead">
		<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1rem">
			<p><span class="im-kind" data-kind="issue">{{icon "mail"}}Newsletter</span></p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Field Notes</h1>
			<p class="im-lede" style="margin: 0">One letter when something lands — what I built, what it cost and what I got wrong. Every letter is also a page here, so nothing is lost to an inbox.</p>
			<div style="max-width: 26rem">{{> "components/subscribe" id="letters-email" button="Subscribe"}}</div>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.issues.length}} letters</span><span>4,210 readers</span><span>62% opened</span><a href="#letters">RSS</a></p>
		</div>
		<div class="im-letterhead-mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 220" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="16" y="40" width="288" height="164" rx="14"/><path d="M16 60 160 150 304 60"/><path d="M16 190 118 118M304 190 202 118" opacity=".6"/><rect x="48" y="12" width="224" height="28" rx="6" opacity=".35"/><circle cx="272" cy="72" r="6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div>
	</header>

	<div class="im-collbar">
		<div class="im-collbar-filters" role="group" aria-label="Which year" data-im-filter="#letters">
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="all" aria-current="page">All</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="2026" aria-current="false">2026</button>
			<button class="im-tag" type="button" value="2025" aria-current="false">2025</button>
		</div>
		<p class="im-hint" style="margin: 0">Newest first</p>
	</div>

	<div class="im-letters" id="letters">
		{{#each demo.issues}}
		<article class="im-letter" data-facet="{{year}}">
			{{#if shot}}
			<span class="im-letter-media"><img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy"><span class="im-letter-n">#{{n}}</span></span>
			{{else}}
			<span class="im-letter-media" style="display: grid; place-items: center"><span class="im-issue-tile" style="position: static"><b>{{n}}</b><strong>{{day}}</strong><span>{{month}}</span><small>{{year}}</small></span></span>
			{{/if}}
			<div class="im-letter-body">
				<p class="im-letter-date">{{sent}}</p>
				<h2 class="im-letter-title"><a href="/collections/newsletter/issue/">{{title}}</a></h2>
				<p class="im-issue-text">{{text}}</p>
				<p class="im-letter-meta"><span>{{words}} words</span><span>{{read}} opened</span></p>
			</div>
		</article>
		{{/each}}
	</div>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap"><div class="im-prose">
<p>A newsletter's head is two columns: the words and the subscribe box on the left, a drawn mark on the right — a letter is not a place, so there is no photograph. No rail on the listing; the rail belongs to a letter. Each letter is an <code>im-letter</code> card with its picture on top and its number on the picture; a letter with no picture keeps the date tile.</p>
</div></section>
